$WIP
BusinessRule The two Uncategorized lines map one to one
Description Corrected. Quicken does not report one Uncategorized line to be
Description split: it reports one in each section, and the split is by the sign
Description of each transaction, not of the category total. So the mapping is
Description one line to one account after all.
Details This was measured rather than assumed, and it is the single rule that
Details decides whether a year reconciles. In 2026 the report shows 104,300.69
Description of Uncategorized under INCOME and 91,331.00 under EXPENSES, netting
Details to 12,969.69. Classifying the net by its sign puts all of it in income
Details and leaves both figures wrong by 91,331.00 with the net still right --
Details which is exactly the shape of error that looks like success.
Details The same rule holds for a category the category list does not declare.
Examples: UncategorizedComparison
| QuickenLine                | OurAccount             | Holds                      |
| Uncategorized under INCOME | Income:Uncategorized   | Amounts above zero         |
| Uncategorized under EXPENSES | Expenses:Uncategorized | Amounts below zero      |

Attributes UncategorizedComparison
| Attribute   | Type        | Default |
| QuickenLine | Text        |         |
| OurAccount  | AccountPath |         |
| Holds       | String      |         |

$WIP
BusinessRule How a Quicken report writes a category tree
Description A parent is a roll-up line and its children sit under it by their
Description last name only, not their full path. Amounts posted to the parent
Description itself appear as "Other <Parent>". A comparison that reads the
Description parent line as a figure of its own double-counts every tree in the
Description report.
Details Measured on the 2025 report: reading parents and children together
Details gives expenses of -297,169.90 against a stated -198,939.00. The lines
Details below are from that report.
Examples: ReportTreeShape
| QuickenLine     | Indent | Means                                  | OurAccount             |
| Auto            | 4      | The roll-up of everything below it     | Expenses:Auto total    |
| Ford Escape     | 8      | A child, by its last name              | Expenses:Auto:Ford Escape |
| Other Auto      | 8      | Posted to Auto itself                  | Expenses:Auto own balance |
| Household       | 4      | A roll-up                              | Expenses:Household total |
| swim pool       | 8      | A child                                | Expenses:Household:swim pool |
| Other Groceries | 8      | Posted to Groceries itself             | Expenses:Groceries own balance |

Attributes ReportTreeShape
| Attribute   | Type        | Default |
| QuickenLine | Text        |         |
| Indent      | Integer     | 0       |
| Means       | String      |         |
| OurAccount  | Text        |         |

$WIP
BusinessRule What each report kind is expected to include
Description Stated because an apparent difference is usually a difference of
Description inclusion rather than of arithmetic, and because the equivalent
Description SimpleAccount report has to be asked for in matching terms.
Details Corrected from the PDFs. An Itemized Categories report does NOT
Details exclude transfers: the all-dates report carries a TRANSFERS section of
Details -63,888.84, and its OVERALL TOTAL is income plus expenses plus that
Details figure. The 2025 and 2026 reports have no such section, because every
Details transfer in those periods has both of its halves inside the report.
Details So a transfer is left out only when it nets to zero within the period,
Details which is not an exclusion rule at all but arithmetic. Our report needs
Details the same section for the comparison to line up.
Examples: InclusionRule
| ReportKind         | Transfers     | InvestmentIncome | MarketValueChange | OurEquivalent                            |
| ItemizedCategories | OwnSection    | Included         | Excluded          | Category report plus a transfers section |
| SpendingByCategory | OwnSection    | Included         | Excluded          | Same                                     |
| CashFlow           | OwnSection    | Included         | Excluded          | Same                                     |
| NetWorth           | NotApplicable | NotApplicable    | Included          | Net worth report at a date               |
| AccountBalances    | NotApplicable | NotApplicable    | Included          | Balances as at a date                    |

Attributes InclusionRule
| Attribute         | Type   | Default |
| ReportKind        | QuickenReportKind | SpendingByCategory |
| Transfers         | String |         |
| InvestmentIncome  | String |         |
| MarketValueChange | String |         |
| OurEquivalent     | String |         |

$WIP
Scenario Transfers are absent from both reports for the same reason
Description Quicken excludes transfers from a category report. SimpleAccount has
Description nothing to exclude: a transfer touches no category, so it cannot
Description appear. The two agree, and they agree by construction rather than by
Description a matching exclusion rule, which is worth one test of its own
Description given there are 8,228 bracketed transfers in the business file.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path              | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking   | Checking   | false       |
| Assets:Savings    | Checking   | false       |
| Liabilities:Visa  | CreditCard | false       |
| Expenses          | Expense    | true        |
| Expenses:Shopping | Expense    | false       |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Payee    | Account           | Amount  |
| T1  | 2025-03-02 | A Shop   | Liabilities:Visa  | -89.99  |
| T1  | 2025-03-02 | A Shop   | Expenses:Shopping | 89.99   |
| T2  | 2025-03-25 | Card     | Liabilities:Visa  | 300.00  |
| T2  | 2025-03-25 | Card     | Assets:Checking   | -300.00 |
| T3  | 2025-03-28 | Transfer | Assets:Checking   | -500.00 |
| T3  | 2025-03-28 | Transfer | Assets:Savings    | 500.00  |
Given the quicken report states : QuickenFigure
| QuickenLine    | QuickenAmount |
| Shopping       | 89.99         |
| TOTAL OUTFLOWS | 89.99         |
When reports compared : QuickenReport Vertical
| Run        | FullYear2025    |
| Book       | business        |
| ReportKind | SpendingByCategory |
| From       | 2025-01-01      |
| To         | 2025-12-31      |
| Lines      | 2               |
Then comparison lines are : ComparisonLine
| QuickenLine    | OurAccount        | QuickenAmount | OurAmount | Difference | Agrees |
| Shopping       | Expenses:Shopping | 89.99         | 89.99     | 0.00       | true   |
| TOTAL OUTFLOWS | Expenses          | 89.99         | 89.99     | 0.00       | true   |
Then comparison summary is : ComparisonSummary Vertical
| LinesCompared   | 2    |
| LinesAgreeing   | 2    |
| LinesDiffering  | 0    |
| OnlyInQuicken   | 0    |
| OnlyInOurReport | 0    |
| TotalDifference | 0.00 |
| Passes          | true |

Attributes QuickenFigure
Description One figure line transcribed from a Quicken PDF.
| Attribute     | Type  | Default |
| QuickenLine   | Text  |         |
| QuickenAmount | Money | 0.00    |

$WIP
Scenario A market value change stays out of the spending report
Description Investment reporting is out of scope this round, but keeping it out
Description of the spending report is not: a revaluation that leaked in would
Description show as income nobody earned. SimpleAccount posts it to Equity,
Description which a category report leaves out. Quicken calls the same thing
Description unrealised gain and also leaves it out. They agree, and because
Description they get there by different routes it is worth one test.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                        | Type       | Placeholder |
| Assets:Portfolio            | Brokerage  | true        |
| Assets:Portfolio:Cash       | Brokerage  | false       |
| Assets:Portfolio:A Fund     | Brokerage  | false       |
| Income                      | Income     | true        |
| Income:Dividends            | Income     | false       |
| Equity:Market Value Changes | Equity     | false       |
Given postings are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Account                     | Amount   |
| T1  | 2025-06-30 | Assets:Portfolio:Cash       | 250.00   |
| T1  | 2025-06-30 | Income:Dividends            | -250.00  |
| T2  | 2025-06-28 | Assets:Portfolio:A Fund     | 1000.00  |
| T2  | 2025-06-28 | Equity:Market Value Changes | -1000.00 |
Given the quicken report states : QuickenFigure
| QuickenLine   | QuickenAmount |
| Dividends     | 250.00        |
| TOTAL INFLOWS | 250.00        |
When reports compared : QuickenReport Vertical
| Run        | FullYear2025    |
| Book       | business        |
| ReportKind | SpendingByCategory |
| From       | 2025-01-01      |
| To         | 2025-12-31      |
| Lines      | 2               |
Then comparison summary is : ComparisonSummary Vertical
| LinesCompared   | 2    |
| LinesAgreeing   | 2    |
| LinesDiffering  | 0    |
| OnlyInQuicken   | 0    |
| OnlyInOurReport | 0    |
| TotalDifference | 0.00 |
| Passes          | true |

