# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What the comparison already shows
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Description The totals below were computed from the QIF export and checked
Description against the PDFs before any of this was implemented in C++. Two of
Description the three periods already agree to the cent.

$WIP
BusinessRule The state of the reconciliation
Description Measured, not predicted.
Details The two years that agree do so exactly, which is what gives any
Details confidence that the date reading, the split signs, the exclusion of
Details transfers, the handling of --Split-- and the per-transaction treatment
Details of uncategorised amounts are all right.
Details The whole period does not agree, and the years it goes wrong in are
Details not known, because there is no Quicken report for any year between
Details 2005 and 2024 to compare against.
Examples: ReconciliationStatus
| Period    | OurIncome  | TheirIncome | OurExpenses | TheirExpenses | Agrees |
| 2026 YTD  | 128684.22  | 128684.22   | -117679.43  | -117679.43    | true   |
| 2025      | 49374.18   | 49374.18    | -198939.00  | -198939.00    | true   |
| All dates | 3162279.50 | 3742439.40  | -2858141.31 | -2715446.00   | false  |

Attributes ReconciliationStatus
| Attribute     | Type    | Default |
| Period        | String  |         |
| OurIncome     | Money   | 0.00    |
| TheirIncome   | Money   | 0.00    |
| OurExpenses   | Money   | 0.00    |
| TheirExpenses | Money   | 0.00    |
| Agrees        | Boolean | false   |

$WIP
BusinessRule Which sections have to be included for a year to reconcile
Description Each of these was established by leaving it out and watching a year
Description stop agreeing.
Examples: SectionNecessity
| Section               | Effect                                                |
| Bank, CCard, Cash     | Nothing reconciles at all                             |
| Invoice and Bill      | 2025 expenses are out by 13,403.46                    |
| Invst, categorised    | A handful of fees and one income line go missing      |
| Invst, securities     | Must be left OUT: including them put 2021 income at 1,430,167.25 against a plausible 130,000 to 190,000 |

Attributes SectionNecessity
| Attribute | Type   | Default |
| Section   | String |         |
| Effect    | String |         |

