# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Figures computed before the reports arrived
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Description These are what SimpleAccount makes of the two QIF files, year by
Description year, written down before any Quicken report for those years had
Description been seen. When the reports arrive the difference is immediate.
Details
Details Writing them first is the point. A figure produced after the answer is
Details known is not evidence of anything, because there is always a plausible
Details adjustment that closes a gap; a figure produced before it is either
Details right or it is a bug with nowhere to hide.
Details
Details Two of these are already checked and agree to the cent: 2025 and the
Details 2026 year to date. The rest are predictions.

Attributes YearFigure
| Attribute   | Type    | Default |
| Book        | Text    |         |
| Year        | Integer | 0       |
| OurIncome   | Money   | 0.00    |
| OurExpenses | Money   | 0.00    |
| OurNet      | Money   | 0.00    |
| Checked     | Boolean | false   |

