$WIP
BusinessRule How a report has to be exported to be comparable
Description Stated because a report run with different settings produces
Description different figures for the same data, and a difference of settings
Description looks exactly like a difference of arithmetic.
Details Every PDF already in testdata was produced this way, which is why they
Details can be compared with each other at all.
Examples: ExportSetting
| Setting     | Value                                               |
| Report      | Itemized Categories                                 |
| Basis       | Cash                                                |
| DateRange   | Custom, 1 January to 31 December of the one year     |
| Accounts    | All                                                 |
| Categories  | All                                                 |
| Subtotal    | None, so the figures are per category               |
| OnePerFile  | One year per PDF                                    |

Attributes ExportSetting
| Attribute | Type   | Default |
| Setting   | String |         |
| Value     | String |         |

