$WIP
Scenario What the import moved is the difference between the two 2026 reports
Description The strongest test of the importer there is. The same report before
Description and after, so the difference is exactly what reading three QFX
Description files did, and it is three figures rather than a thousand rows.
Details An import that duplicated a transaction, or failed to pair a transfer
Details and left it as spending, moves these numbers and nothing else has to
Details be inspected to see it.
Given the quicken reports state : ImportDelta Vertical
| IncomeBefore   | 128684.22  |
| IncomeAfter    | 134034.49  |
| ExpensesBefore | -117679.43 |
| ExpensesAfter  | -155315.28 |
Then import delta is : ImportDelta Vertical
| IncomeBefore   | 128684.22  |
| IncomeAfter    | 134034.49  |
| IncomeMoved    | 5350.27    |
| ExpensesBefore | -117679.43 |
| ExpensesAfter  | -155315.28 |
| ExpensesMoved  | -37635.85  |
| OverallMoved   | -32285.58  |

Attributes ImportDelta
| Attribute      | Type  | Default |
| IncomeBefore   | Money | 0.00    |
| IncomeAfter    | Money | 0.00    |
| IncomeMoved    | Money | 0.00    |
| ExpensesBefore | Money | 0.00    |
| ExpensesAfter  | Money | 0.00    |
| ExpensesMoved  | Money | 0.00    |
| OverallMoved   | Money | 0.00    |

$WIP
Scenario The transaction report confirms that transfers net to zero in the period
Description A second report of the same period, and it is not on a cash basis
Description and does not separate transfers out. Its inflows and outflows are
Description therefore income and expenses plus every transfer, and the two
Description transfer figures must be identical because a transfer is money
Description arriving and leaving inside the same period.
Details They are, exactly: inflows 263,166.89 less income 134,034.49 is
Details 129,132.40, and outflows 284,447.68 less expenses 155,315.28 is
Details 129,132.40. That is why the 2026 Itemized Categories report has no
Details TRANSFERS section while the all-dates one does.
Details This is the cross-check worth having, because it tests the transfer
Details handling from a direction the category report cannot.
Given the quicken reports cross check : TransferCrossCheck Vertical
| Inflows  | 263166.89  |
| Outflows | -284447.68 |
| Income   | 134034.49  |
| Expenses | -155315.28 |
Then transfer cross check is : TransferCrossCheck Vertical
| Inflows          | 263166.89  |
| Outflows         | -284447.68 |
| Income           | 134034.49  |
| Expenses         | -155315.28 |
| TransfersIn      | 129132.40  |
| TransfersOut     | -129132.40 |
| TransfersNetZero | true       |
| NetTotal         | -21280.79  |

Attributes TransferCrossCheck
| Attribute        | Type    | Default |
| Inflows          | Money   | 0.00    |
| Outflows         | Money   | 0.00    |
| Income           | Money   | 0.00    |
| Expenses         | Money   | 0.00    |
| TransfersIn      | Money   | 0.00    |
| TransfersOut     | Money   | 0.00    |
| TransfersNetZero | Boolean | false   |
| NetTotal         | Money   | 0.00    |

