$WIP
Scenario The same QFX imported into both gives the same report
Description This is the second half of the acceptance test and it checks the
Description importer rather than the migration. The QFX goes into a Quicken
Description file that already holds the history, and into a SimpleAccount book
Description migrated from the same history, and the two reports are compared
Description again.
Details So it is not only a test of reading OFX. It is a test of what the
Details import does when it meets twenty years of existing transactions: the
Details FITID test, the match-on-amount-and-date test, and the choice between
Details creating a transaction and clearing one that is already there. Those
Details are the rules in ImportOfx that a small file cannot exercise.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                   | Type    | Placeholder |
| Assets:Checking        | Checking | false       |
| Expenses               | Expense | true        |
| Expenses:Groceries     | Expense | false       |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | Expense | false       |
Given imported postings are : ImportedPostingRow
| Ref | Date       | Payee  | Account            | Amount  | Cleared   | FitId |
| T1  | 2026-09-15 | Shop A | Assets:Checking    | -100.00 | Uncleared | none  |
| T1  | 2026-09-15 | Shop A | Expenses:Groceries | 100.00  | Uncleared | none  |
Given import target is : ImportTarget Vertical
| AccountPath | Assets:Checking |
When transactions imported : OfxTransactions
| TrnType | DatePosted | Amount  | FitId | Name   | Memo | CheckNum |
| DEBIT   | 2026-09-16 | -100.00 | F1    | SHOP A | none | none     |
| DEBIT   | 2026-09-20 | -60.00  | F2    | SHOP C | none | none     |
Then import summary is : ImportSummary Vertical
| New       | 1 |
| Duplicate | 0 |
| Matched   | 1 |
| Possible  | 0 |
Given the quicken report states : QuickenFigure
| QuickenLine   | QuickenAmount |
| Groceries     | 100.00        |
| Uncategorized | 60.00         |
When reports compared : QuickenReport Vertical
| Run        | AfterQfx        |
| Book       | business        |
| ReportKind | SpendingByCategory |
| From       | 2026-01-01      |
| To         | 2026-10-03      |
| Lines      | 2               |
Then comparison summary is : ComparisonSummary Vertical
| LinesCompared   | 2    |
| LinesAgreeing   | 2    |
| LinesDiffering  | 0    |
| OnlyInQuicken   | 0    |
| OnlyInOurReport | 0    |
| TotalDifference | 0.00 |
| Passes          | true |
# The matched transaction did not become a second 100.00, which is what would
# show here as 200.00 against Quicken's 100.00. That is the failure this run
# is for.

