$WIP
BusinessRule In what order the comparisons are run and what stopping means
Description Each is only worth running when the one before it has passed.
Examples: RunOrder
| Order | Run          | DependsOn    | AFailureHereMeans                                 |
| 1     | WholePeriod  | The migration | Something did not come over, or came over twice  |
| 2     | FullYear2025 | WholePeriod   | A transaction is in the wrong year                |
| 3     | CurrentYear  | FullYear2025  | The two programs bound a part-year differently    |
| 4     | AfterQfx     | CurrentYear   | The importer duplicated or dropped a transaction  |

Attributes RunOrder
| Attribute   | Type          | Default     |
| Order       | Integer       | 0           |
| Run         | ComparisonRun | WholePeriod |
| DependsOn   | Text          |             |
| AFailureHereMeans | Text    |             |

